ty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8c6e450-fe10-5923-accc-8b824e3c81c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-18047" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨5,9⟩.$ Find $|\\,a\\,|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(9)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{106}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186233595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6b4ebe4-9baa-5ff0-847a-49d99ba69795" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26fce79e-92f6-594d-aec2-af45c6145c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18048" :question/problem "if $a=⟨-4,8⟩$, then  what is the magnitude of  $a?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}
